        "CBRS"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Last week, a short seller, @CulperResearch, published a report arguing that @cerebras wafers wear out after about two years, and based on that premise the report suggested that the economics of our business are fundamentally challenged.  \n\nThat number is wrong, and given that the basis of the entire report is built upon that assumption, all of the assertions that follow are also wrong.\n\nWe do agree that the question of how long our systems last is a fair question, so we want to address the topic plainly.   \n\nIf you have a few minutes, I would encourage you to click on the link below, which wil",
      "url": "https://x.com/andrewdfeldman/status/2118344222558552167",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 14:06:34 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Citadel in October: Tech companies created an AI bubble reminiscent of the dot-com crash.\n\nCitadel in November: “The setup has improved” \n\nEarnings continue to beat while AI infrastructure valuations compressed sharply.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118272043288547413",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 09:19:45 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Why does it take some random anime character on X to push back against AI narratives?\n\nWhen you have all these companies worth billions, or even trillions, staying silent while their valuations crash.\n\nDepressed valuations does in fact trigger reflexive pressure on financing and counterparty confidence.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118262426101547280",
      "time": "Thu Nov 05 08:41:32 +0000 2026",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": false
