      "text": "Cyberoffense/defense is probably going to eat up a TON of compute and end up a continuous compute-intensive arms race. \n\nEven $AMZN CEO thinks cybersecurity would take up 20% of tokens consumed for the next year. \n\nIt's literally a problem of how much you throw at compute for vulnerability discovery + model capability, from of my chats w/ Horizon3. \n\nAnd this is going to become a nation state issue, as seen with the implications already with PHP to vulnerabilities with banks/infrastructure from AI swarms. \n\nBut people see this and throw money at $CRWD, $NET, and others, which I was saying was ",
