      "text": "For companies like $SIVE / $AAOI, the demand imbalance for lasers are so severe\n\nThat even a 20-30% overall demand reduction from a hypothetical DC slowdown would likely not eliminate the shortage. \n\nWe're seeing this before the next architectural shifts, where $NVDA Jensen Huang expects 15x optical volume for CPO scale-up. \n\nAnd as more hyperscalers commit to NPO as seen with $LITE new $5B UHP laser contracts. \n\nI'd argue this is more nuanced since I can't say the same for finished 800G/1.6T pluggables or lower end 70mW-100mW laser ranges that are currently bottlenecks. \n\nBut this argument is",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2118035778253283768",
